
SHORTCUTS

1.0 Introduction

Shortcuts can be found in the directory Zeus:Shortcuts/

Shortcuts are small ARexx scripts, which may be executed from the Shell or
from their Workbench icons, to perform tasks on your Zeus Bulletin Board.

Shortcuts in general are simply interfaces to one or more Zeus functions,
but they enable new users to use the more advanced features of Zeus with
the minimum of fuss.

They also provide useful tutorial to new users regarding how different
binaries, scripts and ARexx functions should be called, for the time when
you will want to customise Zeus to your more exact standards.

All Shortcuts require Zeus to be running, as they rely on the presence of
the Zeus ARexx port.


1.1 Configuration

To maintain flexibility, Shortcuts can be configured on the command line
and through direct keyboard input. The command line options will allow
shortcuts to be set up as regularly scheduled tasks.


1.2 Customising Shortcuts further

Shortcuts are not intended to be a limiting factor in the customisation
of your Zeus Bulletin Board, rather the opposite. If you have a bright
idea to make a function more useful, or wish to incorporate the function
into a larger script of your own, we recommend you make a copy of the
Shortcut into another drawer and start playing with the script.


2.0 The Shortcuts

2.1 Shortcut Directories

Shortcuts are split up into directories most descriptive of their function.
The four main subdirectories are:

 o Zeus:Shortcuts/File/
 o Zeus:Shortcuts/Message/
 o Zeus:Shortcuts/User/
 o Zeus:Shortcuts/BBS/

The File subdirectory caters for Shortcuts directly related to the
manipulation of the file database, including maintenance and statistics.

The Msg subdirectory caters for Shortcuts related to all aspects of the
message sub-system, including importing/exporting, database maintenance,
statistics.

The User subdirectory caters for maintenance and manipulation of the
User database.

The BBS subdirectory caters for Shortcuts which affect the BBS' running
as far as the users are concerened.


2.2 Executing Shortcuts

Shortcuts can be executed by simply clicking on their icon on the
Workbench screen. A window will popup and execute the ARexx script. Make
sure the ARexx launcher, "rx", is in your system path. "rx" is located
in SYS:Rexxc/ on most Amigas.

The Shortcut scripts may also be executed through a Shell, allowing
you to pass them arguments, bypassing any input while executing.

The scripts all use the extension ".zsc" and are located in the same
directory as their icon.


2.3 Shortcut Descriptions

Supplied with Zeus are the following shortcuts:

 o BBS/ChristmasSpecial.zsc

   - This script is intended to reward your users at Christmas time, by
     setting all the file areas to mark file transfers as "free". This
     means that their ratios will cease to take effect. Running this
     script will prompt to turn "Christmas Special" on or off.

     Arguments: ON|OFF

 o RebuildCatalogues.zsc

   - This script performs a complete, intensive rebuild on the file
     catalogue. It may take some time to complete.
     A path to a backup directory may be specified, where the old
     catalogues will be copied to in the event of data loss.

     Arguments: [Path to backup directory]

 o RenumberCatalogues.zsc

   - This script renumbers the file catalogue, starting at 1.
     It will then invoke a FileRebuild to recreate the index files.
     It may take some time to complete.
     A backup directory for index files may also be specified.

     Arguments: [Path to backup directory]

 o TrimBases.zsc

   - This script trims all the message areas until they contain 'MaxMsgs'
     as defined in the Message Area Configuration

     Arguments: n/a

 o RebuildUsers.zsc

   - Rebuilds the user base, deleting all user directories and records
     that no longer exist.

 o StripUsers.zsc
 
   - Deletes all users that haven't called in 'n' days.

     Arguments: [Days]


3.0 Default Header

All shortcuts have the following template.

/*
** Zeus Shortcut Script
**
** <Name of Script>
**
** <Script Description>
** <Argument Template>
**
** <Copyright Message>
*/

If you are creating a shortcut to distribute to other Zeus users, try
sticking to this template format.

